       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation alone doesn't change my concern, because 1000 mg of sertraline daily has no recognized indication. It is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. I can't see a clinical scenario where it would help this patient, and it could seriously harm them.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If it's a typo or a misremembered dose:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 100 mg or 200 mg, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If there's a specific reason for the high dose:** Please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy first. If they approve a dose above the labeled maximum, it should go through your hospital's override or high-dose approval process, with the rationale documented.\n- **If this is a possible overdose or ingestion:** This needs a different approach, not a scheduled order. Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology can advise on monitoring and management.\n\nI'm glad to help with any of these, including a lower-dose order or a note for pharmacy."
      }
